changelog: |
  0.2.0: consumed by reference. The kit is now ALSO a Claude Code plugin
  (`spec-driven`, published by the hub's root .claude-plugin/marketplace.json):
  the chain and the autopilot as namespaced skills (/spec-driven:specify …
  :evolve, lifted from law-ai's prompts/ and genericized), the backlog-triager
  agent, and hooks/hooks.json wiring gate-check.sh with ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}.
  The CI half is the hub's reusable .github/workflows/spec-gate.yml (caller
  template in workflows/), and fleet-kit.sh is the one file a consumer vendors
  so `make lint-specs` can run the hub's tools from a parent hub checkout or a
  cached sparse clone. tools/evolve_audit.py (law-ai's discovery audit,
  genericized: TODO scan, missing docs, Cobertura coverage; the LegalBench scan
  stays in law-ai's own harness) joins the tools; its pre-kit copy is archived.
  gate-check.sh resolves the plugin's tools first, then tools/ or scripts/.
  UPS-WORK-07 accepts a `uses:` of spec-gate.yml as the gate job. law-ai is the
  first by-reference consumer (its prompts/, scripts/ gates, .claude chain
  commands, hook and evolve workflow were deleted in the same change).
  0.1.0: initial kit. The AO-SDLC gates (spec validator, backlog lint, id
  minter, evolve picker, gate-check hook) lifted from bamr87/law-ai (the
  superset) and genericized: every tool takes `--root`, the hook finds tools/
  or scripts/, and law-ai's hard-coded constitution §13 ranking check becomes
  data in an optional specs/_review_questions.json (review-questions.example.json
  reproduces it exactly). Run against law-ai and gitorio, the kit tools give
  output identical to each repo's own copy, and law-ai's
  tests/test_specs_and_backlog.py and tests/test_backlog_picker.py pass with
  the kit copies swapped in.
  archive/ holds byte-exact copies of the pre-kit tools from both repos
  (stamp 0.0.0) so an upgrader can tell an untouched copy from a hand-edited one.
notes: The four tools/*.py gate files are byte-identity files (UPS-WORK-07) for any repo that still vendors them; a by-reference consumer vendors only fleet-kit.sh (byte-identical too). Repo-specific behaviour lives in specs/_review_questions.json. Templates (spec/plan/tasks, BACKLOG, constitution) are seeded once and then owned by the repo. plugin.json `version` tracks this file's `version` (the kit test asserts it).
